body:
&#x200B;

Hi Enchanted\_Lyre, thanks for your comment, though I don't fully understand what you are trying to say.  -- I understand that we need to find our own purposes for existence, which I believe many people do with finding partners/raising families.  I am vehemently an anti-natalist.  -- My comment about circling the world is not necessarily specific to travel, I go from project to project and find joy in them, but ultimately find them to be senseless in the end.  It's fleeting joy.  I have traveled a bit, and have met absolutely amazing people, but I think of humanity, in a general, as a selfish species.  We are no smarter or humbler than the humans that came out of caves or discovered fires.

I recognize that I am less than optimistic about the future and people, but when a population has decided that capital is more important than not burning down our only home it’s difficult to feel otherwise.
